From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:17:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: expose Location URL attributes as unforgeable own
 properties

Bind href, search, hash, pathname, hostname, host, port, origin and protocol
as enumerable, non-configurable own accessors using the existing
LegacyUnforgeable binding support. Keep getter, setter and navigation
behavior unchanged.

Sephora copies window.location through an Object.keys-based helper. The
prototype-only bindings produced a copy without pathname, causing
isCustomerServicePage() to throw while checkout helper 39776 was being
initialized and leaving the server-rendered Add to Basket button disabled.
With the native bindings fixed, the actual proxied product page mounts
React and enables the button without a JavaScript shim or button mutation.

Update the two existing Location setter assertions to inspect the instance
rather than Location.prototype. No new upstream tests are added.

Reference: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#the-location-interface
Validation: release build and all 1658 upstream tests pass. Captured Sephora
location-copy code now succeeds in both Chrome and Lightpanda. The live
proxied SKU 2968907 page returns HTTP 200 and has an enabled basket button
at all three observations. Other existing page errors remain out of scope.
---
 src/browser/tests/window/location.html |  4 ++--
 src/browser/webapi/Location.zig        | 19 ++++++++++---------
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/browser/tests/window/location.html b/src/browser/tests/window/location.html
index 17e38a7..283e9c6 100644
--- a/src/browser/tests/window/location.html
+++ b/src/browser/tests/window/location.html
@@ -25,11 +25,11 @@
 </script>
 
 <script id=location_pathname_setter>
-  testing.expectEqual('function', typeof Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(Location.prototype, 'pathname').set);
+  testing.expectEqual('function', typeof Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(location, 'pathname').set);
 </script>
 
 <script id=location_search_setter>
-  testing.expectEqual('function', typeof Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(Location.prototype, 'search').set);
+  testing.expectEqual('function', typeof Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(location, 'search').set);
 </script>
 
 <div id="sec1"></div>
diff --git a/src/browser/webapi/Location.zig b/src/browser/webapi/Location.zig
index 488e19c..a9a8417 100644
--- a/src/browser/webapi/Location.zig
+++ b/src/browser/webapi/Location.zig
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
